{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>For all flesh had corrupted their way</b>. If we interpret \"all flesh\" literally, and say that even beasts, wild animals, and birds corrupted their way by mating with other species, as Rashi explained (Rashi on Genesis 6:12), then we would say \"for the earth was filled with violence because of them\" — not because of all of them, but because of some of them, and Scripture would be recording the punishment of man alone. Alternatively, we would say that they did not maintain their proper order in this respect either, so that every beast became predatory and every bird became raptor-like, and thus they too commit violence. But according to the plain sense, \"all flesh\" means all mankind. Further on, Scripture interprets \"all flesh in which is the spirit of life\" (Genesis 7:15) and \"of every living thing of all flesh\" (Genesis 19) as every living creature in a body, but here \"all flesh\" means all mankind. Similarly, \"all flesh shall come to bow down before Me\" (Isaiah 66:23), and similarly \"when flesh has on its skin\" (Leviticus 13:24)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "The citation 'Genesis 19' refers to Genesis 6:19; the Hebrew text reads 'בראשית ו:י\"ט' which is 6:19, and the verse reference was rendered accordingly."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:25:31.457906725Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}